# Symbol budget

Default: **net symbol count stays flat or shrinks** on every change slice. Growing the surface needs **explicit user permission** (e.g. “add `FloorQty`”, “ok to add symbols”).

**Counts as a symbol** — any named entity you introduce or export: types, functions, methods, `constexpr`, globals, namespace-scope names. Not counted: locals, lambdas, anonymous-namespace internals, private members unless they become new public API.

**Free without permission** — rename (1:1 = net zero), repurpose (same type, new fields/meaning), modify body/signature, remove dead code. Repurposing a struct: replace fields; don’t add fields on top of stale ones.

**Net math** — per task: removes + renames offset adds. Remove three, add one → OK. Unsure → inline or extend existing names; ask before net growth.

# C++ headers

- **Few exported names** — entry + shared state/data only.
- **No one-liner wrappers** — inline; don’t add a name without real logic.
- **Struct when shared** — pass snapshot `const&` between sites; no return bags.
- **One read pass** — load shared state once, pass downstream.
- **Concrete over generic** — unroll fixed sequences; abstract when N or direction varies.
- **Split files** only when a second real caller exists — not for planned work.

Before adding a name: used in >1 place or stable API? non-trivial? can’t stay readable inlined? Any **no** → don’t add it. Symbol budget still applies — passing the checklist is not permission to grow net count.

# Comments

- Short; on new/changed code.
- **Why** or non-obvious invariant — not what the line does.
- Prefer one line.

```cpp
// BAD: increment counter
++n;

// GOOD: single-writer gate — one eval per burst
if (gate.exchange(1) != 0) return;
```
